{
 "idea": {
  "id": "rsi2_pullback",
  "family": "reversal",
  "title": "Buy a sharp two-day dip in a stock that is in an uptrend, hedged with the market",
  "why": "In a rising stock a sharp short dip is more often profit-taking than a change of story, and buyers who missed the move step in. Connors' RSI(2) rule is the popular form. It differs from the plain reversal trade in being long only, conditioned on trend, and judged against the stock's own history rather than against other stocks.",
  "source": "Connors and Alvarez 2009; widely traded, so likely crowded",
  "market": "us",
